  "body": "Stacked on #2808 (merge #2808 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nAdd `camcraft_geometry::nesting::cut_order` for one placed sheet.\nBuild a global containment forest for closed loops and open chains.\nResolve closed `Auto` sides by depth parity and open `Auto` sides to `OnLine`.\nTraverse the forest iteratively. Sort siblings by enclosed area, then stable ID.\nSchedule marking, internal, rough profile, and final breakthrough phases.\nUse an explicit `release_phase` to distinguish blind pockets from through cuts.\nRefuse invalid geometry, side requests, incomplete schedules, and cuts after material release.\nReport circular-tool corner limits without changing the picked geometry.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe geometry crate lacked one cut order across a nested sheet.\nAn enclosing hole can free a smaller part before that part's cuts finish.\nIndependent operation orders cannot enforce that sheet relationship.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe initial pinning build failed on unchanged upstream base `f3b0e1955` with `E0432` because the planner API was absent.\nThe tested stacked base is parent commit `1947b6b6c30d214baf3db2072f95ed51ccb2dae3` from #2808.\n\nAll 17 pins pass:\n\n- `sheet_tree_cuts_parts_in_holes_before_release_and_small_siblings_first`\n- `sheet_pass_phases_keep_marking_first_and_breakthrough_last`\n- `sheet_refuses_a_phase_that_frees_a_hole_before_its_nested_part`\n- `sheet_order_validator_refuses_released_ancestors_missing_and_extra_passes`\n- `sheet_order_validator_checks_global_phases_but_accepts_safe_sibling_orders`\n- `sheet_order_validator_names_unrequested_and_duplicate_open_passes`\n- `sheet_refuses_a_later_pass_after_the_same_contour_releases`\n- `sheet_blind_pocket_pass_keeps_material_until_final_breakthrough`\n- `sheet_refuses_invalid_release_phase_requests`\n- `sheet_open_chain_sides_resolve_and_invalid_sides_name_the_chain`\n- `sheet_refuses_invalid_width_ids_and_pass_requests`\n- `sheet_refuses_degenerate_self_crossing_and_retraced_geometry`\n- `sheet_refuses_area_accumulation_overflow_by_name`\n- `sheet_refuses_crossing_or_touching_contours_and_boundary_crossing_chains`\n- `sheet_crossing_open_features_keep_the_same_containing_parent`\n- `sheet_corner_limits_use_tool_radius_and_ignore_input_winding`\n- `sheet_open_side_corner_limits_follow_the_directed_cut_side`\n\nEach of 21 runtime guard mutations failed its pins. Each restored version passed again.\nThe mutations covered:\n\n- Width, duplicate IDs, pass requests, release requests, mandatory breakthrough release, and open/closed side requests.\n- Minimum vertices, finite coordinates, coordinate bounds, zero-length segments, open closure, retracing, self-crossing, boundary crossing, and area overflow.\n- Unknown cuts, extra or duplicate passes, global phase order, released material, and missing passes.\n\nThe area mutation used wrapping addition. Only the new overflow pin failed; the other 16 pins passed.\nThe spiral fixture checks positive and negative overflow in a valid 642-vertex loop.\nCopying the upstream nesting entry back failed with `E0432`. Restoring the stacked entry passed all 17 pins.\nThe four planner/test files stayed byte-identical when the branch moved onto #2808.\nThe stacked branch passed the focused pins and the upstream-entry mutation again.\n\nValidation:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry --test nesting_cut_order`: 17 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: batch fallback, 937 steps, zero failures.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n\n## Current-head validation (2026-11-21)\n\nHead: `8c6090b27e67f251e999bb9bc4f5bcbd5fe723dd`.\nThis head merges `upstream/main` into the branch. The merge has no conflicts and no hand edits (class SAME).\nThe merge gives the branch the light tier. The source of the PR is not changed.\n\n- Light: `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main` passed: 3 steps, zero failed, 1.7 minutes.\n  `motion light: lib` and `motion light: adaptive_troch_parallel` passed.\n- Heavy: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` passed: 236 steps, zero failed, 19.4 minutes.\n  The motion and app heavy lanes ran.\n  Six known fails were red as expected: three for #1950 and three for #2849. The gate accepted each of them.\n- Quick: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed: 1042 steps, zero failed, 19.0 minutes.\n  The final clippy step (`--all-targets -- -D warnings`, all touched crates, `camcraft-geometry` included) passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone in the #2159 commit. It changes no `.nc` or `.cl` files.\nThe direct comparison with newer upstream also shows eight upstream-only Explain fixtures added by #2793:\n`carvera.nc`, `grblhal.nc`, `sinker-iso.nc`, `sinumerik.nc`, `tinyg.nc`, `tormach-lathe.nc`, `tormach-plasma.nc`, and `wire-iso.nc`.\nThese are under `crates/post/tests/golden/explain/`. The child patch does not change or delete them.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe tests did not cover placement-to-planner adapters, posted output from this planner, or physical machine execution.\nThe current-head validation section records the light, heavy and quick results. Pixel snapshots were not run.\nThe branch contains `upstream/main` from the merge in head `8c6090b27`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2808 rewrites `crates/geometry/src/nesting.rs`, including its header and module declarations.\nThis branch starts at parent commit `1947b6b6c`.\nThe #2159 change in that file adds the `cut_order` export beside the placement API.\nMerge #2808 first. Refresh this child after the parent merges.\n\nEffort: max; no escalation.\n\nChangelog: Add deterministic sheet cut order with material release checks, cut-side resolution, and cutter corner diagnostics.\n\nFixes #2159\n",
